  "review": [
    "Previous goal turn added checked project data bindings and produced an input-pinned full comparison; that was progress. This batch uses that snapshot to correct native caller behavior in seven cards and one helper.",
    "The widened scan compares basic-block-local constant arguments for every uniquely paired callee, instead of restricting itself to a small handpicked API list. It screens 6,076 eligible nonexact functions and finds eleven constant-argument candidates.",
    "Five outlast findings are rejected after inspecting both callee prologues: native reads all nine formals from stack arguments; rebuilt uses EAX/EDX/ECX for player/card/event and omits constant-zero color arguments. Same numeric stack offsets therefore describe different formals. The source mana costs are retained.",
    "Abandoned Sarcophagus, As Foretold, Lurrus and Fires of Invention have distinct query and activation paths. Only ten helper calls in the activation-list branches change to EVENT_ACTIVATE; ten query calls retain EVENT_CAN_ACTIVATE. Fresh compiled calls verify both value multisets against the native stream.",
    "Lost Legacy passes flag 4 to lobotomy_effect, reporting only cards exiled from hand and allowing partial selection. Its source previously required every copy and reported the wrong draw count. The existing name filter and draw consumer are preserved.",
    "The Opposition Agent tutor destination passes MPCFE_FOR_CMC (2) to its exile permission instead of free casting (1). All native player/zone operands and surrounding lifecycle operations remain as before.",
